Third-party colour palettes
===========================

The JSON files in this directory are vendored verbatim from openchamber:

    https://github.com/openchamber/openchamber
    packages/ui/src/lib/theme/themes/
    Copyright (c) 2025 Bohdan Triapitsyn
    MIT

They are copied rather than depended on because they are data, not code: a dependency would
put a package resolution between a reviewer and a hex value, and preman does not ship them at
runtime — `scripts/generate-themes.ts` reads them once, by hand, and the audited result is what
is committed under `src/renderer/appearance/themes/`.

Verbatim also means unformatted: this directory is in `.prettierignore`, so re-vendoring is a
readable diff instead of a reflow.

openchamber's files are themselves ports of upstream colour schemes. Each generated theme module
carries its own `source` and `licence` fields, taken from the table below, and the settings pane
shows them. Every scheme is MIT except JetBrains, which is Apache-2.0.

    Aura                    daltonmenezes                       MIT
    Ayu                     dempfi                              MIT
    Carbonfox (Nightfox)    EdenEast                            MIT
    Catppuccin              Catppuccin                          MIT
    Dracula                 Zeno Rocha                          MIT
    Fields of the Shire     openchamber                         MIT
    Flexoki                 Steph Ango                          MIT
    gruvbox                 morhetz                             MIT
